The official wasm-bindgen release is now a fixed reference catalogue
entry pinned to the existing 0.2.127 binding ABI. The latest 0.2.130
release introduces a second major version of syn and was rejected by
the unchanged dependency gate. The matching Linux CLI archive was
fetched with `cargo download wasm-bindgen-release` and verified against
both the upstream checksum file and release asset SHA-256
61d4a7dc85acfa0d2354ccc0b8361928c7e52a746d17f28ebaa795ed3dc1614a.
The CLI is not installed or executed automatically by the downloader.

The WebAssembly save-slot adapter now uses browser local storage with
a dedicated 1-to-64-byte ASCII namespace and numeric slots. It bounds
the raw JavaScript string before transferring it into Rust and rejects
noncanonical text, malformed envelopes and excess sizes using the
shared portable save contract. Each write replaces one origin-local
value. Successful writes report unsupported crash durability instead
of a filesystem sync guarantee; quota, disabled storage, browser
eviction and same-origin writers remain limitations.

