host event scheduling, rendering and input adapters.

The existing browser save diagnostic now exercises the shared
DisplayStore, VolumeStore and ControlStore wrappers over one explicit
origin-local preference namespace. It alternates integer/windowed and
fill/fullscreen preference values, 75% and 50% volume, and bounded ASCII
and UTF-8 control text. Each publication reports unsupported crash
durability. Separate incompatible typed payloads are rejected by every
wrapper on both load and replacement, preserving their exact raw bytes.
Empty and oversized control text is rejected without changing the
saved settings. These are persisted values, not applied browser
fullscreen, audio or control bindings.

