A further isolated negative control on the committed keyboard module
rejected the third listener registration. Each invocation failed
before dispatching events and removed the two already installed
listeners. The subsequent unmodified run passed. The injected error
checks partial subscription cleanup, not a naturally failing browser.

Read-only browser capability probes on 2026-11-26 inform subsequent
adapter work. Firefox 160.0 created Canvas2D and WebGL2 contexts and
returned the expected pixel samples, including a WebGL2 context
requested with failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat. The renderer identified
llvmpipe rather than physical GPU acceleration. A separate DOM probe
observed two synthetic touch identities, inclusive edge and centre
positions, motion beyond the canvas rectangle, cancellation and
release. The canvas had a 180 by 90 CSS rectangle and 360 by 180
backing pixels; synthetic pointer capture threw NotFoundError.
This is host API availability only, not Rust rendering or touch
admission, trusted capture, high-DPI hardware or gameplay evidence.

An isolated OfflineAudioContext probe rendered 128 frames of synthetic
stereo samples at 48 kHz and independently compared both output
channels to the inputs. The samples matched exactly. No audible
output or realtime playback was attempted. The synchronous PCM queue
contract still needs a browser adapter that respects asynchronous
activation, backpressure, suspension and teardown. No audio
distribution or physical playback acceptance is inferred.
